                <pb facs="0930" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6625/33–36.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Wright to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-08-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 364.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you herewith
                    an English translation, clipped from the semiofficial Japan Times of the 5th,
                    6th, and 7th instants, of the text of the convention, with the additional
                    articles and protocol annexed to the same, signed by the Japanese and Russian
                    Governments at St. Petersburg on May 31 last in regard to the connection in
                    Manchuria of the Chinese Eastern and the South Manchurian railways. I have as
                    yet been unable to obtain a copy of the original French text of this
                    convention.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Luke E. Wright.</hi></signed></closer>





